  "question": "A moving coil galvanometer has coil resistance $20\\Omega$ and gives full-scale deflection for a current of $5\\text{ mA}$. Calculate the shunt resistance required to convert it into an ammeter of range $0.5\\text{ A}$.",
  "options": {
    "A": "$S=\\dfrac{I_gG}{I+I_g}=\\dfrac{(5\\times10^{-3})(20)}{0.5+5\\times10^{-3}}\\approx0.198\\,\\Omega$.",
    "B": "$S=\\dfrac{IG}{I-I_g}=\\dfrac{(0.5)(20)}{0.5-5\\times10^{-3}}\\approx20.2\\,\\Omega$.",
    "C": "$S=\\dfrac{I_gG}{I-I_g}=\\dfrac{(5\\times10^{-3})(20)}{0.5-5\\times10^{-3}}\\approx0.202\\,\\Omega$.",
    "D": "$S=\\dfrac{G}{I-I_g}=\\dfrac{20}{0.495}\\approx40.4\\,\\Omega$."
  },
